 "summary": "The Rayleigh-formula definition is faithful: `-dslope (deriv f) 0` equals `-f'(x)/x` exactly because each iterate is proven even (so `f'(0) = 0`), and `deriv_reducedSphericalBesselJ` states that identification on the whole line. I re-derived `j_0 = sinc`, `j_1 = sin x/x\u00b2 - cos x/x`, the `(2l+3)` recurrence, the `1/(2l+1)\u203c` origin coefficient, the raising/lowering pair, and the ODE independently; all match A&S \u00a710.1 and DLMF \u00a7\u00a710.47/10.51/10.52, and the whole-line and `x = 0` edge cases are true as stated.",
